*Proof.* As  $D'Q'$  is tangent to  $\omega$ ,  $D'$  lies on the polar of  $Q'$ . But  $EF$  is the polar of  $A$ , so  $Q'$  lies on the polar of  $A$  and vice versa by La Hire's. Thus,  $AD'$  is the polar of  $Q'$ , so we must have  $IQ=IQ'\perp AD'$ , as desired.  $\blacksquare$ **<span style="color:#f00">Claim:</span>**  $IM\parallel AD'$ .

